From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Pfeiffer <cpfeiffer@rev-crew.info>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 02:43:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] Fix DHooks params of a second setup of a detoured
 function

UpdateRegisterArgumentSizes gives the params of a setup the sizes of
the registers they're passed in, which GetParamStruct lays out the
parameter buffer by. Native_EnableDetour only called it for the setup
that creates the detour, though. Another setup of the same function,
e.g. of another plugin, or a second DynamicDetour of the same plugin,
kept the sizes it declared, and read its params in registers at the
wrong offsets of the buffer.

Call it for every setup that enables a detour. It doesn't change the
detour's calling convention: the sizes it sets there are the same each
time.

On its own, this shows on x86_64 with params in registers, whose sizes
(8) differ from the declared ones (4 for an int). With the patch of
register params' values on Windows, which has the params learn the
registers that x86_64's calling convention assigns them, it's every
param in a register: without this, a second setup of a function reads
them wrongly while the first one reads them right.

Tested with Day of Infamy's 64-bit Windows server (srcds_x64):
- Under Wine (wine-cachyos 10.0), DHooks built with clang-cl and xwin's
  MSVC libraries: two DynamicDetours of
  CINSRules::GetTotalActivePlayersOnTeam(int) with a post callback each
  read team for a call with 3. With the patch of register params only,
  the first reads 3, the second -1072758784; with this patch as well,
  both read 3.
- On Windows 11, built with MSVC 14.52 (Visual Studio 2026), both
  setups read 3 already with the patch of thiscall detours without
  params alone: the wrong values come from whatever the registers hold,
  which differs between clang-cl's and MSVC's builds, so the bug
  doesn't show there with this test. With the whole series, both read 3
  there as well.
- On Linux x86, where only params with a custom register are concerned,
  the dedicated server plays coop rounds with its detours (doi-config's
  round test) with DHooks built with the DHooks patches as with DHooks
  built from master.
---
 extensions/dhooks/natives.cpp | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/extensions/dhooks/natives.cpp b/extensions/dhooks/natives.cpp
index f52c95a1..17938124 100644
--- a/extensions/dhooks/natives.cpp
+++ b/extensions/dhooks/natives.cpp
@@ -431,10 +431,13 @@ cell_t Native_EnableDetour(IPluginContext *pContext, const cell_t *params)
 	{
 		ICallingConvention *pCallConv = ConstructCallingConvention(setup);
 		pDetour = pDetourManager->HookFunction(setup->funcAddr, pCallConv);
-		if (!UpdateRegisterArgumentSizes(pDetour, setup))
-			return pContext->ThrowNativeError("A custom register for a parameter isn't supported.");
 	}
 
+	// Every setup needs the sizes and registers of its params, not only the one that created the
+	// detour: another setup of the function, e.g. another plugin's, reads its params with them.
+	if (!UpdateRegisterArgumentSizes(pDetour, setup))
+		return pContext->ThrowNativeError("A custom register for a parameter isn't supported.");
+
 	// Register our pre/post handler.
 	pDetour->AddCallback(hookType, (HookHandlerFn *)&HandleDetour);
 
